        25["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Living Crystal</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Extends the existing endless<br />world, inventory, clock and<br />commands. New-world<br />geography, local indexed heat<br />and shared propagated<br />physical light, proportional<br />exposure damage, tending,<br />renewable wild colonies, a<br />pure chapter-availability<br />policy with effective tool<br />caps and canonical action<br />locks until activation,<br />paused optional automation<br />with preserved earned state,<br />intrinsically lightproof<br />facility interiors without<br />shutter controls/state,<br />heat-sensitive contents and<br />exposed-cargo light damage,<br />protected material<br />condition/storage/transfer,<br />and three physical<br />dormant-machine repairs plus<br />safe activation, permanent<br />completion and empty-handed<br />next worlds. Dedicated<br />catalog identities provide<br />bespoke<br />chamber/cooler/vault/conduit/machine/equipment<br />sprites and five machine<br />restoration states in the<br />existing row renderer. Legacy<br />terrain/rules and saves are<br />retained.</div>"]
        style 25 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        26["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Layered World</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Coordinates and key packing<br />(x, y, z), tile rules as data<br />(TILE_INFO), and chunked<br />terrain: the forest surface<br />at z = 0 from noise octaves,<br />solid geology below with one<br />shaft per chunk. Chunks are<br />generated lazily and<br />LRU-cached; player edits<br />(richness mods), per-layer<br />fog and the holes between<br />layers live outside the<br />cache. Explored chunks and<br />observed resource types have<br />derived spatial indexes,<br />including one/two-unit<br />reserve masks that remove<br />exhausted deposits from<br />searches; Map/Set-compatible<br />geometry and prop<br />notifications invalidate<br />dependent light fields and<br />charger candidates.</div>"]
        style 26 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        27["<div style='font-weight: bold'>State and Saves</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>createState() builds the<br />state; serialize/deserialize<br />write and validate a JSON<br />save (its format is<br />WORLD_FORMAT in format.js,<br />frozen so every world is<br />kept; saves from format 10 on<br />load, and the browser sets<br />aside, never overwrites, one<br />it can't read). state.events<br />is transient and never saved.</div>"]
        style 27 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        28["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Simulation Step</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>step(s, dt): production,<br />logistics, abundance income,<br />battery and the burning<br />flare; movement and fog<br />reveal as far as your light<br />reaches (sightRadius).<br />Browser and AUTO hosts enable<br />cumulative solo production<br />after Logistics: grouped<br />rates, cached counts/mastery,<br />command/query settlements,<br />and buffer snapshots at saves<br />or rate changes. Visual<br />events query nearby tile<br />buckets. Cultivation runs<br />local environment deadlines<br />at 250ms in the same<br />canonical step. Chunk-cached<br />sky/artificial illumination<br />follows rock and open ladder<br />connections; direct sky<br />columns retain strength,<br />diffuse paths attenuate, and<br />local dependency invalidation<br />rebuilds fields from<br />surviving sources. Carried<br />fields change only at source<br />tile/strength changes. Sun<br />phases reuse sky access;<br />rendering and proportional<br />crystal exposure consume the<br />same field, with player<br />awareness and remembered<br />exploration separate. Battery<br />intervals support quiet-tick<br />batching and reuse nearby<br />charger candidates with exact<br />range and daylight checks.<br />Reveal compares exact circle<br />row intervals and visits<br />newly covered edges. Resource<br />streams settle together with<br />targeted manual balance<br />updates. Variable-step/shared<br />callers and extreme<br />arithmetic retain the legacy<br />economy.</div>"]
        style 28 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        29["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Actions</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Harvest (gather deposits on<br />the surface, dig rock<br />underground), Trail sweep<br />targets, collect, and build;<br />plus travel between layers<br />through holes (dig down from<br />the forest, climb up through<br />the ceiling, drop through<br />holes and shafts). All<br />personal world actions share<br />interaction.js: walkable<br />same-layer contact on the<br />object's tile or a cardinal<br />side; no diagonal or distant<br />reach. Collection empties one<br />contacted building.<br />Infrastructure remains<br />independent of player<br />contact.</div>"]
        style 29 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        30["<div style='font-weight: bold'>AUTO Brain</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>nextIntent(s, mind): legal<br />player actions from explored<br />terrain, remembered<br />observations, visible mine<br />glints, own resources and<br />public rules. Integer A*<br />treats unseen underground<br />rock as an assumption and<br />replans after normal<br />revelation, without<br />inspecting hidden geology.<br />Unseen chargers, ladders,<br />shores and tunnel props<br />cannot steer decisions.<br />Prices building repayment<br />against required upgrades;<br />mining is a fallback only<br />when surface acquisition is<br />unavailable, includes passive<br />income and return travel and<br />targets useful observed<br />finds. Waits at Embark, and<br />never spends Insight in<br />shared worlds. Selected known<br />chargers alone authorize<br />charging decisions. Manual<br />holds share AUTO cadence.<br />Pure: mind caches<br />observations and routes.</div>"]
        style 30 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        31["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Stockpile</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>What you own as piles around<br />home, on a logarithmic scale:<br />one pile per unit of the two<br />leading digits (at most 18<br />per resource), each power of<br />ten its own kind; from 10^7 a<br />pile covers a square of tiles<br />one wider per power, as far<br />as its slot allows. Home<br />ground is a square laid out<br />like a town: roads cross in<br />the middle and each resource<br />owns a block with fixed slots<br />(the leading digit in the<br />corner by the crossroads, the<br />second along the outer<br />edges), so nothing stands<br />outside home ground or on<br />another pile. Pure: only a<br />picture of the inventory.</div>"]
        style 31 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        32["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Catalog</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Everything that exists in the<br />game, by the id its pictures<br />are kept under: tiles,<br />resources, buildings, the<br />wanderer, marks, buttons,<br />upgrades, perks and colours,<br />each with what it does and<br />its picture slots. Built from<br />the other content tables, so<br />a new tile or upgrade can't<br />go undocumented.</div>"]
        style 32 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        33["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Economy and Upgrades</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Content tables, costs and<br />multipliers, and one registry<br />of every purchase (tools,<br />refineries, the Abundance<br />Engine, unlocks, perks) that<br />buying, the progression map<br />and the sheet all share; the<br />ledger (current production<br />including crystal chambers,<br />waiting stock and estimated<br />resource payback);<br />spending.js records actual<br />categorized payments with<br />explicit partial history for<br />old saves. Stoneworks<br />supplies a non-stacking<br />same-owner quarry bonus<br />within two tiles. A derived<br />tile index caches service<br />links per layout; both scalar<br />and event economies use<br />instance rates. Physical solo<br />depots use an eight-tile<br />same-owner/layer collection<br />index; overlapping depots<br />never duplicate transfers.<br />Also embark/prestige and the<br />goal track.</div>"]
        style 33 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
      end

